```python
def f(): pass
f.__qualname__  # 'f'
```

Yes. And a lambda at module level has `__qualname__` = `<lambda>`. So the `<locals>` prefix is only added when the function scope's parent is itself a function scope (i.e., nested functions). Let me re-check: in CPython 3.11+ compiler:

```c
if (scope_type == COMPILER_SCOPE_CLASS) {
